course: dictionary
lesson: 1340
title: Camp: a place, a verb, a group
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A camp is a place where people stay in tents or cabins, often outdoors. «They camped on a remote common far from habitations.» Here camped is a verb, the action of setting up tents and staying outdoors.
explain: Camp can be a noun (a place) or a verb (an action). Look at the small words around it. «Summer camp» and «base camp» name places. «Set up camp» and «camp out» show something people do.
explain: A camp can also be a group of people who share an idea. Read the clues around the word: if the sentence talks about tents, food and nights outside, it means the place. If it talks about people who think the same way, it means the group.
fact: A camp is a place where people stay in tents or cabins.
fact: A «summer camp» is a place where children go in the holidays to do activities.
fact: «Camp out» means to stay outdoors in a tent.
fact: «In bear country, store food in bear-proof containers and keep a clean camp, because bears follow food smells.»
fact: Church groups may run camps and holiday clubs full of games, stories and adventures.
exercise: «They camped on a remote common far from habitations.» What does camped mean here? | Swam in the sea | *Stayed outdoors in tents | Walked quickly past the houses | Sold things at a market
exercise: In bear country, why should you keep a clean camp? | *Because bears follow food smells | Because camps must be painted white | Because bears like bright colours | Because tents need washing every day
exercise: What does «summer camp» mean? | A tall tower built on a hill | A cold shop that sells ice | *A place where children go in the holidays to do activities | A lesson about numbers at school
test: In «Camping means living outdoors for a while», what kind of word is camping? | A kind of tent | The opposite of home | A noun for a place | *A form of the verb camp, showing an action
test: What does «base camp» most likely mean? | A camp at the bottom of the sea | *The main camp that a group works from | A shop that sells sweets | A group of hungry bears
exam: A family camps in bear country; what must they do with their food? | *Store it in bear-proof containers | Throw it on the campfire | Leave it out on the table | Feed it to the bears
